  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>This shield was the last thing standing at a gate whose name is forgotten. Its face is dented in a hundred places, and each dent is polished bright by the hands of soldiers who touch it before a battle.</p><p>You have a +3 bonus to Armor Class while you wield this shield.</p><p><strong>Stand Between.</strong> When a creature within 5 feet of you takes damage, you can use your Reaction to take that damage in its place. Nothing reduces the damage you take this way.</p><p><strong>Unbroken.</strong> Once per day, when you take damage, you can use your Reaction to take none of it. The shield regains this power at dawn.</p><p><strong>The Honest Threshold.</strong> Hung above a door, gate or bridge, the shield lets no one cross with a lie. Whoever speaks falsely to get past it finds that the words will not come out. It does not stop silence, and it does not stop force.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
